---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Areas Covered" description="Towns and areas covered by JR's Heating and Cooling.">
  <h1>Areas we cover</h1>
  <p class="lead">[List of towns/postcodes you actually serve.]</p>

  <div class="placeholder">
    <strong>Important — read before adding area pages:</strong> per the setup
    guide's "critical rule for area pages" (Section 2), don't create a page
    per town with only the town name swapped — Google filters that out as
    thin content. Each area page needs a real job done there, something true
    about the local area, and (ideally) a named local testimonial. Build
    three or four properly once you have that material, rather than one for
    every town up front.
  </div>
</Layout>
